<bpmn:definitions xmlns:bpmn="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/MODEL" xmlns:bpmndi="http://www.omg.org/spec/BPMN/20100524/DI" xmlns:dc="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DC" xmlns:di="http://www.omg.org/spec/DD/20100524/DI" id="Definitions_PA-128.1-ai-strategy-governance-framework-model-risk" targetNamespace="https://erpplans.local/bpmn" exporter="erpplans generate-bpmn.py" exporterVersion="1.0">
    <bpmn:process id="W_W3929" name="W3929. AI/ML Strategy, Operating Model &amp; Governance Framework" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Digital/data strategy (links to VS-28/VS-113); AI-program review
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: 1 enterprise AI-governance program
Owner: AI Governance Lead / CIO
Participants: AI Governance, Data &amp; Analytics (links to VS-28/VS-30.2), Enterprise Architecture (links to VS-113), IT/Security (links to VS-27/VS-27.3), Privacy/DPO (links to VS-91), Legal (links to VS-100), Risk/Internal Audit (links to VS-21), HR (links to VS-19/VS-103), business AI owners (Fraud links to VS-125, CDP links to VS-126, S&amp;OP links to VS-127, Marketing links to VS-14, LP links to VS-23)
Source: workflow W3929 — AI/ML Strategy, Operating Model &amp; Governance Framework</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3929_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3929_Lane1" name="AI Governance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3929_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3929_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3929_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3929_Lane2" name="CIO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3929_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3929_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3929_Start4" name="Digital/data strategy (links to VS-28/VS-113); AI-program review">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3929_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3929_Task5" name="AI Governance/CIO define the enterprise AI strategy and governance framework…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AI Governance/CIO define the enterprise AI strategy and governance framework: the AI-use-case portfolio and roadmap, the governance operating model (AI steering, AI ethics review board, model-risk function), alignment to enterprise architecture (links to VS-113) and data strategy (links to VS-28), and the framework baseline (ISO 42001 AI Management System, NIST AI RMF)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / CIO / EA
Accountable (A): CIO / CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3929_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3929_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3929_Task6" name="AI Governance establish the governance scope and boundaries: which AI/ML is in…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AI Governance establish the governance scope and boundaries: which AI/ML is in scope (incl. vendor and GenAI), the risk-tiering approach, the interaction with privacy (links to VS-91), security (links to VS-27.3), audit (links to VS-21), and legal (links to VS-100), and the AI value/KPIs (model count, value, incidents, fairness pass-rate)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Risk / Privacy / Legal
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3929_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3929_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3929_Task7" name="CIO/Executive ratify the strategy and governance, approve the AI budget (links…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CIO/Executive ratify the strategy and governance, approve the AI budget (links to W3935), and cascade accountability to business AI owners
Responsible (R): CIO / CIO
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3929_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3929_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3929_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3929_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3929_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-614 (ensure controlled execution — AI Strategy, Governance Framework &amp; Model Risk Management (PA-128.1).); CTL-147 (ensure AI model risk &amp; human-oversight control — cross-reference.) | - operational: central AI-governance framework; operational: ISO 42001/NIST AI RMF baseline
Owner: AI Governance Lead / CIO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3929_Assoc10" sourceRef="W3929_Annotation9" targetRef="W3929_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3929_Flow11" sourceRef="W3929_Start4" targetRef="W3929_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3929_Flow12" sourceRef="W3929_Task5" targetRef="W3929_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3929_Flow13" sourceRef="W3929_Task6" targetRef="W3929_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3929_Flow14" sourceRef="W3929_Task7" targetRef="W3929_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
    <bpmndi:BPMNDiagram id="W3929_diag">
      <bpmndi:BPMNPlane id="W3929_plane" bpmnElement="W_W3929">
        <bpmndi:BPMNShape id="W3929_Lane1_di" bpmnElement="W3929_Lane1" isHorizontal="true"><dc:Bounds x="160" y="80" width="950" height="170" /></bpmndi:BPMNShape>
