        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AI Governance define AI/ML roles and RACI: business use-case owner (accountable for outcome), data-science builder (links to VS-30.2), model-risk validator (independent — 2nd line links to VS-21), internal audit (3rd line links to VS-21), and the AI governance function (oversight)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / CIO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3933_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3933_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3933_Task5" name="AI Governance operate the three lines of defense: 1st line…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AI Governance operate the three lines of defense: 1st line (build/operate/monitor), 2nd line (model risk/policy challenge), 3rd line (independent audit), with clear separation between model builder and validator
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Model Risk / Audit
Accountable (A): CIO / Head of Internal Audit &amp; Risk
Duration: Maintained</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3933_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3933_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3933_Task6" name="AI Governance/HR define AI-competency/talent needs (links to VS-19.4/VS-123)…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AI Governance/HR define AI-competency/talent needs (links to VS-19.4/VS-123), and ensure role assignments don&#x27;t create unacceptable conflicts of interest
Responsible (R): AI Governance / HR
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3933_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3933_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
