    <bpmn:process id="W_W3936" name="W3936. AI Maturity Assessment &amp; Continuous Improvement" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual review; maturity cycle
Frequency: Annual + quarterly improvement
Volume: 1 AI-maturity assessment/yr
Owner: AI Governance / CIO
Participants: AI Governance, CIO, Strategy (links to VS-33), Risk/Internal Audit (links to VS-21), Data &amp; Analytics (links to VS-28), business AI owners, Innovation (links to VS-30)
Source: workflow W3936 — AI Maturity Assessment &amp; Continuous Improvement</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3936_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3936_Lane1" name="AI Governance">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3936_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3936_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3936_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3936_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3936_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3936_Start3" name="Annual review; maturity cycle">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3936_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3936_Task4" name="AI Governance/CIO run the annual AI-maturity assessment (strategy, governance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: AI Governance/CIO run the annual AI-maturity assessment (strategy, governance, data, platform, talent, responsible-AI, value — vs ISO 42001/NIST AI RMF maturity), benchmark vs retail peers, and identify gaps
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Strategy / Risk
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3936_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3936_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3936_Task5" name="AI Governance develop the maturity-improvement roadmap (governance depth links…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: AI Governance develop the maturity-improvement roadmap (governance depth links to W3930, model-risk links to W3932, responsible-AI links to W3937–W3944, monitoring links to W3947), prioritized with executive sponsorship
Responsible (R): AI Governance / Strategy
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3936_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3936_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3936_Task6" name="AI Governance execute quarterly improvement actions, track maturity…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: AI Governance execute quarterly improvement actions, track maturity progression, and report to the executive committee and Audit Committee (links to VS-33/VS-36)
Responsible (R): AI Governance / CIO
Accountable (A): CIO
Duration: Quarterly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3936_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3936_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3936_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3936_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3936_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-614 (ensure controlled execution — AI Strategy, Governance Framework &amp; Model Risk Management (PA-128.1).) | - operational: annual assessment and exec sponsorship; operational: balanced roadmap
Owner: AI Governance / CIO</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
